  "summary": "Richmond City Council voted 5-2 to renew and expand its contract with Axon for CCTV, drones, and other surveillance services, replacing Flock Safety as primary vendor, but delayed a decision on a separate ALPR contract for the second time over data security and efficacy concerns. The city has been searching for a new ALPR vendor since Chief Tim Simmons disabled Flock cameras last year after discovering the 'national lookup' feature exposed Richmond's data to outside agencies.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Richmond has been searching for a new ALPR vendor since February after Richmond Police Chief Tim Simmons disabled Flock's cameras late last year out of concern for data security.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "Simmons said the department used the feature to search outside the city's data but were not informed by Flock that enabling \"national lookup\" also allowed outside agencies to access Richmond's data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "The benefits are unproven and the harms are documented",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
